 # Tetrahedral representation and traversal
-Also called: Projected tetrahedra, cell projection with tetrahedral decomposition, tetrahedral mesh traversal
+
+Also called: Projected tetrahedra, cell projection, tetrahedral volume rendering
 
 ## Overview
-This family covers methods that represent volumetric data as a collection of tetrahedra to facilitate rendering, primarily by projecting these primitives to screen space or traversing them in object space. It solves the problem of rendering unstructured or irregular tetrahedral grids, which lack the regular connectivity of voxel grids, by leveraging the geometric simplicity of tetrahedra (planar faces, linear interpolation) [S1, S2, unofficial][S3][S4, S6, S7][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16][S17, S18, unofficial]. It differs from [Tetrahedral Volume Rendering](820-tetrahedral-volume-rendering.md) by explicitly using geometric projection and scan-conversion rather than pure ray casting, and from [GPU-based Projected Tetrahedra](7484-gpu-based-projected-tetrahedra.md) by encompassing both software and hardware-accelerated sorting/projection variants [S2, unofficial][S4, S6, S7][S12, unofficial][S14, S16].
+Tetrahedral representation and traversal is a family of object-order volume rendering techniques that decompose volumetric data into tetrahedral cells to resolve topological ambiguities and enable hardware-accelerated rasterization or efficient ray traversal [S1, S2, unofficial][S3][S4, S6, S7][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16][S17, S18, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering unstructured or curvilinear grids by projecting 3D tetrahedra into 2D screen space (or traversing them in object space) and compositing the results in back-to-front order [S1, S2, unofficial][S4, S6][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16][S17, S18, unofficial]. Unlike ray-casting methods that sample scalar fields directly, this family relies on explicit geometric projection and subdivision [S2, unofficial][S4, S6, S7][S12, unofficial][S14, S16].
 
