 - **Definition:** Calculates the projected area of a tetrahedron in normalized screen space to determine refinement criteria or culling [S1, unofficial]. Uses cross products to compute wedge areas, which are twice the triangle area, then divides by four [S1, unofficial].
-- **Steps:** Project tetrahedron vertices $T, L, R, B$ to screen space using camera projection: $T \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(T)$, $L \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(L)$, $R \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(R)$, $B \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(B)$ [S1, unofficial]. Calculate area sum using cross products of vertex vectors: $\text{area} \leftarrow |(L-T)\times(R-T)| + |(R-T)\times(B-T)|$ [S1, unofficial]. Add remaining terms: $\text{area} \leftarrow \text{area} + |(B-T)\times(L-T)| + |(L-B)\times(R-B)|$ [S1, unofficial]. Return final area divided by 4: $\text{return area} / 4$ [S1, unofficial].
